{"id": "EUVD-2026-103516", "enisaUuid": "ee8c48a5-b7ae-3d5a-b552-0f4d67a38e90", "description": "Schroedinger libschroedinger through 1.0.11 contains a divide by zero vulnerability that allows attackers to crash applications by supplying a zero slice_bytes_denom or slice count in a Dirac stream. Attackers can provide a crafted low-delay picture parsed by schro_decoder_parse_transform_parameters and schro_decoder_parse_lowdelay_transform_data to trigger a SIGFPE and cause denial of service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T02:17:56", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/schroedinger-lowdelay-quant-matrix-oob", "https://github.com/Distrotech/schroedinger/blob/schroedinger-1.0.11/schroedinger/schrodecoder.c#L2932", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/schroedinger-libschroedinger-through-1.0.11-divide-by-zero-in-low-delay-transform-parsing"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-112054", "GHSA-5cjc-2hj8-3x6x"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.12, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1a1bad1c-4ab2-3aec-874e-0ed2cea1cba9", "product": {"name": "schroedinger", "vendor": {"name": "Schroedinger"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.0.11"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "e358f4a7-56d9-3560-bcbe-1cd6908472a1", "vendor": {"name": "Schroedinger"}}], "isExploited": false}